{"name":"Momentum","hex":"#746f5c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"momentum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Of a body in motion: the tendency of a body to maintain its inertial motion; the product of its mass and velocity, or the vector sum of the products of its masses and velocities.","Strength or force gained by motion or movement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/momentum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Momentum","blocks":[{"text":"In Newtonian mechanics, momentum is the product of the mass and velocity of an object. It is a vector quantity, possessing a magnitude and a direction. If m is an object's mass and v is its velocity, then the object's momentum p is: \nIn the International System of Units (SI), the unit of measurement of momentum is the kilogram metre per second (kg⋅m/s), which is dimensionally equivalent to the newton-second."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Billard.JPG/330px-Billard.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momentum","wikidata":"Q41273"},{"title":"Momentum (organisation)","blocks":[{"text":"Momentum is a British left-wing political organisation which has been described as a grassroots movement supportive of the Labour Party; since January 2017, all Momentum members must be members of the party. It was founded in 2015 by Jon Lansman, Adam Klug, Emma Rees and James Schneider after Jeremy Corbyn's successful campaign to become Labour Party leader and it was reported to have between 20,000 and 30,000 members in 2021."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momentum_(organisation)","wikidata":"Q22079985"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Elastischer_sto%C3%9F_2D.gif/330px-Elastischer_sto%C3%9F_2D.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Elastischer_sto%C3%9F_2D.gif/330px-Elastischer_sto%C3%9F_2D.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two-dimensional elastic collision. There is no motion perpendicular to the image, so only two components are needed to represent the velocities and momenta. The two blue vectors represent velocities after the collision and add vectorially to get the initial (red) velocity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElastischer_sto%C3%9F_2D.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/1950_%22Avicenna%22_stamp_of_Iran_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-1950_%22Avicenna%22_stamp_of_Iran_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/1950_%22Avicenna%22_stamp_of_Iran_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/1950_%22Avicenna%22_stamp_of_Iran_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-1950_%22Avicenna%22_stamp_of_Iran_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ibn Sīnā (980–1037)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1950_%22Avicenna%22_stamp_of_Iran_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Frans_Hals_-_Portret_van_Ren%C3%A9_Descartes_%28cropped%292.jpg/330px-Frans_Hals_-_Portret_van_Ren%C3%A9_Descartes_%28cropped%292.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Frans_Hals_-_Portret_van_Ren%C3%A9_Descartes_%28cropped%292.jpg/330px-Frans_Hals_-_Portret_van_Ren%C3%A9_Descartes_%28cropped%292.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"René Descartes (1596–1650)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrans_Hals_-_Portret_van_Ren%C3%A9_Descartes_(cropped)2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://